# matrix-label-formatter — implementation plan

> Requirement: `/workspace/requirements/matrix-label-formatter.yaml`
> `fix(matrix): fix matrix label formatter does not work`

---

## 1. Goal

`matrix.x.label.formatter`, `matrix.y.label.formatter`, `matrix.body.label.formatter`,
`matrix.corner.label.formatter` (and the per-cell overrides
`matrix.x/y.data[i].label.formatter`, `matrix.body/corner.data[i].label.formatter`)
are currently **completely ignored**. The matrix view always renders the raw cell value.

Two concrete defects:

1. **Runtime**: `MatrixView#createMatrixCell` builds the label text as `textValue + ''` and hands
   it to `setLabelStyle` as `opt.defaultText`, without a `labelFetcher`. `getLabelText()` in
   `src/label/labelStyle.ts` only reads `normalModel.get('formatter')` **inside the
   `if (labelFetcher)` branch**, so with no fetcher the formatter is never read.
2. **Typing**: `MatrixCellStyleOption['label']` is typed as the plain `LabelOption`, which has
   **no** `formatter` member at all (it is explicitly commented out in `src/util/types.ts`), so
   even declaring a formatter is a TS error for TS users.

After the fix:

* a **string** formatter is expanded as a simple template (`'{name}'`, `'{value}'`, `'{coord}'` …)
  via `formatTplSimple`;
* a **function** formatter is invoked and its (non-null) return value is used as the label text;
* the callback receives a documented params object:
  `{componentType: 'matrix', componentIndex, name, value, coord, $vars}` where `coord` is the
  `[xLocator, yLocator]` pair already used for the matrix tooltip (`MatrixXYLocator[]`);
* a new public type `MatrixLabelOption` / `MatrixLabelFormatterParams` is exported from
  `src/coord/matrix/MatrixModel.ts` and used for `MatrixCellStyleOption['label']`, so the option
  is type-checked.

---

## 2. Findings (current code)

### 2.1 The label text is hard-wired to the raw value

`/workspace/src/component/matrix/MatrixView.ts:282-301`

```ts
    let cellText: Text | NullUndefined;

    if (textValue != null) {
        const text = textValue + '';
        _tmpCellLabelModel.option = cellOption ? cellOption.label : null;
        _tmpCellLabelModel.parentModel = parentLabelModel;

        setLabelStyle(
            cellRect,
            // Currently do not support other states (`emphasis`, `select`, `blur`)
            {normal: _tmpCellLabelModel},
            {
                defaultText: text,
                autoOverflowArea: true,
                // By default based on boundingRect. But boundingRect contains borderWidth,
                // and borderWidth is half outside the cell. Thus specific `layoutRect` explicitly.
                layoutRect: clone(cellRect.shape)
            },
        );
```

`text` is `const` and is never passed through any formatter. `setLabelStyle` is called with an
`opt` that has **no `labelFetcher`**.

### 2.2 `setLabelStyle` only honours `formatter` when a `labelFetcher` exists

`/workspace/src/label/labelStyle.ts:144-169`

```ts
function getLabelText<TLabelDataIndex>(
    opt: SetLabelStyleOpt<TLabelDataIndex>,
    stateModels: LabelStatesModels<LabelModel>,
    interpolatedValue?: InterpolatableValue
): Record<DisplayState, string> {
    const labelFetcher = opt.labelFetcher;
    const labelDataIndex = opt.labelDataIndex;
    const labelDimIndex = opt.labelDimIndex;
    const normalModel = stateModels.normal;
    let baseText;
    if (labelFetcher) {
        baseText = labelFetcher.getFormattedLabel(
            labelDataIndex, 'normal',
            null,
            labelDimIndex,
            normalModel && normalModel.get('formatter'),
            ...
        );
    }
    if (baseText == null) {
        baseText = isFunction(opt.defaultText)
            ? opt.defaultText(labelDataIndex, opt, interpolatedValue)
            : opt.defaultText;
    }
```

`normalModel.get('formatter')` is read **only** inside `if (labelFetcher)`. Matrix supplies none,
so the formatter is silently dropped and `opt.defaultText` (the raw value) wins.

### 2.3 `label` option type has no `formatter`

`/workspace/src/coord/matrix/MatrixModel.ts:190-206`

```ts
export interface MatrixCellStyleOption {
    // [NOTE - padding]:
    ...
    label?: LabelOption;
    itemStyle?: ItemStyleOption;
    cursor?: string;
    // By default, auto decide whether to be silent, considering tooltip.
    silent?: boolean | NullUndefined;
    // Used when style conflict - especially for thick border style.
    z2?: number;
}
```

and `/workspace/src/util/types.ts:1283-1303`:

```ts
export interface LabelOption<
    TNuance extends {positionExtra: unknown} = {positionExtra: never}
> extends LabelCommonOption {
    ...
    // TODO: TYPE not all label support formatter
    // formatter?: string | ((params: CallbackDataParams) => string)
}
```

`MatrixCellStyleOption` is the base of `MatrixDimensionOption`, `MatrixBodyOption`,
`MatrixCornerOption`, `MatrixBaseCellOption`, `MatrixDimensionCellOption` and
`MatrixBodyCornerCellOption` (see `MatrixModel.ts:135-155` and `:147-169`), so a single change
there covers every place a matrix label can be declared.

### 2.4 Runtime proof of the bug (executed against the current tree)

A throwaway jest run (jsdom, `test/ut/jest.config.cjs`) with

```js
matrix: {
    x: { data: ['A', 'B'], label: { formatter: 'Col: {name}' } },
    y: { data: ['X', 'Y'], label: { formatter: (p) => '<' + p.name + '>' } }
}
```

collected the attached text contents of the matrix view group and produced
`["A","B","X","Y"]` — the raw values. The function formatter was **never called**.

### 2.5 The `xyLocator` pair that must be surfaced as `coord`

`createMatrixCell` already receives the locator pair and forwards it to the tooltip:

